# Density Compare
# Radium (Ra) — real density 5.5 g/cm³. equal masses: Radium vs water — sides ∝ (1/ρ)^(1/3).
scene "Radium Density Compare"

element_cube = cube 11.3mm color: #00ff9d at (-20mm, 5.7mm, 0)
water_cube = cube 20mm material: water at (18mm, 10mm, 0)
# both cubes weigh the same: about 43.9 g — the water cube is the reference
